#### Problem Description
The issue arises when attempting to access the `chunks` attribute of a Zarr-backed xarray dataset. Instead of lazily loading the chunk information, the entire dataset is loaded into memory. This behavior is unexpected and contrary to the intended lazy loading mechanism.

#### Root Cause
The root cause of the issue is in the `get_chunksizes` function defined in `xarray/core/common.py`. Specifically, the function checks if the `data` attribute of a variable has a `chunks` attribute using `hasattr(v.data, "chunks")`. However, this check triggers the loading of the entire dataset into memory because it indirectly calls the `values` property of the `Variable` class, which converts the data to a NumPy array.

